# Frontend Rules

## API Base URL — Single source of truth
// frontend/src/config.js  ← create this file, import it everywhere
export const API_BASE = "http://localhost:8000/api";

## The 5 Views — Tab Names and Route Paths
| Tab Label | Component File | Route |
|---|---|---|
| 🗺️ National Map | MapView.jsx | / |
| 📊 County Dashboard | CountyDashboard.jsx | /county/:name |
| 🔬 Simulation | CounterfactualView.jsx | /simulate |
| 📋 Benchmarks | BenchmarkTable.jsx | /benchmark |
| ⚙️ Methodology | MethodologyView.jsx | /methodology |

## Color System (Tailwind classes only, no hex anywhere in JSX)
- High score (>75): green-600, bg-green-100
- Mid score (50-75): yellow-500, bg-yellow-100
- Low score (<50): red-500, bg-red-100
- Primary brand: emerald-700
- Background: gray-50
- Card background: white, shadow-md, rounded-xl

## Chart Components — Recharts Only
- Score timeline: <LineChart> with <Line> for historical (solid) and forecast (strokeDasharray="5 5")
- Confidence band: <Area> with opacity 0.2 for 5-95% CI
- Pillar breakdown: <RadarChart> with <Radar>
- Uplift comparison: <BarChart> with two <Bar> (baseline=gray, counterfactual=emerald)
- Variance explained: <BarChart> horizontal

## Every API-Fetching Component Must Have
const [data, setData] = useState(null);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
const [error, setError] = useState(null);
// Show <Spinner /> while loading, <ErrorCard message={error} /> on error

## Counterfactual Slider Component — Two-Phase Interaction Model
- Range: -20 to +20 (represents percentage change, i.e. -0.20 to +0.20)
- Display: "−20%" to "+20%" with 0 center mark
- Phase 1 — ON EVERY SLIDER CHANGE (lightweight, instant):
    POST /api/pillars/preview with current {county, interventions}
    → Update the before/after radar chart immediately (pure matrix math, no STGNN)
    → Show delta badges: "Reproductive Efficiency ▲ +0.34" next to each pillar axis
    → Label clearly: "Pillar Impact Preview — before STGNN propagation"
    → Debounce at 150ms to avoid flooding the API during fast slider drags
- Phase 2 — ON "RUN SIMULATION" CLICK ONLY (heavy, STGNN inference):
    POST /api/counterfactual with all slider values / 100
    → Show loading spinner during inference
    → Render score trajectory chart, uplift bars, and two-stage XAI explanation
    → "Run Simulation" button is disabled until at least one slider is non-zero

## Two-Stage XAI Explanation Component (XAIExplanation.jsx)
Renders two visually distinct sections using `pillar_shifts` and `explanation` from API response:
  🔧 Stage 1 — "What your intervention changed" (feature → pillar):
     Show which raw features were adjusted and which pillars moved as a result
     Source: pillar_shifts field from /api/counterfactual response
  🤖 Stage 2 — "What the model predicted" (pillar → score):
     Show the STGNN-computed score gain and note spatial graph propagation
     Source: uplift field + explanation string from /api/counterfactual response
Use emerald color for positive pillar shifts, red for negative, gray for unchanged

## PillarRadar Component — Reused in Two Places
- View 2 (County Dashboard): single radar, single year, sourced from /api/pillars/{county}
- View 3 (Simulation): dual radar — before (gray) and after (emerald) overlaid on same chart
  When used in View 3: receives {before: {P1,P2,P3,P4}, after: {P1,P2,P3,P4}} as props
  Animate the transition from before to after when preview API responds

## View 5 — Methodology Panel Rules
- Metrics table must be clearly labeled: "Phase A7 — Held-out 2025 Evaluation"
- Add a "Two-Model Architecture" card explaining:
    Eval Model (stgnn_eval_weights.pt) → honest performance measurement
    Forecast Model (stgnn_forecast_weights.pt) → retrained on all data for deployment
- CVAE validation chart: per-year comparison (5 separate sub-charts or tabs), NOT a global average
- Augmentation card: show "5 real snapshots → 25 training snapshots" with plain-language explanation

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase
- Hooks: useCamelCase (e.g., useCountyData.js)
- API functions: camelCase in frontend/src/api.js (single file for all fetch calls)
- Preview calls: previewPillarShift(county, interventions) in api.js
- Simulation calls: runCounterfactual(county, interventions, horizon) in api.js
